OGO_BLACK (https://d586LZ04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/W5+113/d586L=\r\nZ04/VWJVH825FTDDN6YlKLdJ5Vy1W6mk3Cf5HxRnbN8XrLG83pyd0W7Y8-PT6lZ3prW12GgzF15=\r\nr4X8W1nKsjN6B8NnRW8Y1mj_6zXxKrW2rbsfV5ncXcKW7J4wzS7Pvtz8W2BM3yl7DL2MdW4Th2Z=\r\n86ck5BJW2K981Q5fQf2MW6S9tX-9fg6m5W2_ZvLc8gvKP1VVZVtm2C1cBgW8lbtrN3_wZN5W8WT=\r\nSJg8YfxmrVHFFdb7svgc9N1DGgCPY5DjwW64K3dC1kC8JsW5P6-mP1nK13WW1WQXzx5KWZ9jW2_=\r\nwxnD6PHdJXVtgmLB45BnpYW47HS-h1FZ3TNW2r3vPf1ZtvwzW1FYln59gxzfKW60mx9P65PsSQW=\r\n1cW67Z3kH6w9W7vwYLx3PvJRdf9l0Zvs04 )\r\n\r\nPicture this.\r\n\r\nIt=E2=80=99s late. You=E2=80=99re brushing your teeth. The day starts repla=\r\nying in your head.\r\n\r\nNotice what shows up.\r\n\r\nThe awkward comment. The thing you didn=E2=80=99t finish. The decision you=\r\n=E2=80=99re still second-guessing.\r\n\r\nThat=E2=80=99s negativity bias (https://d586LZ04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/W=\r\n5+113/d586LZ04/VWJVH825FTDDN6YlKLdJ5Vy1W6mk3Cf5HxRnbN8XrLGs3pyd0W8wLKSR6lZ3=\r\nnrW7F-K0S5cK9hCW8F3wJw5SMH7LW6553VT1dMGQ6N4d8GX24x63KN7cLmwZJSpD1W7hpLNz3Qm=\r\nm5wN8X_7BcwK-qZW1W-KLv6XtJzBVYFRLH1xxbrrW1X8zpG6-SfJgW4Yfc10204LH4W5l0z7q4q=\r\nZ_y-W7mLcT08_8dJwW89rFd61mTlZlW5gmrnV6KPFCLN7ln8wSq3h2bW3vpL0h5MTdsBW1W9GKr=\r\n5149VXW8t1hY18Y9bMTW44QbnD6JtQwpN8hqJPph2Fz8N7Zn5D029JhrN5fmkc0Vt_RCW4rRdhR=\r\n76RcCnW7hLkqQ5-8d_mW5jChhC5NWPtNW74-phv4V6YJZW6sVV5G99hXdxf7T18nj04 ) , and=\r\n it=E2=80=99s doing what it does best.\r\n\r\nI bet most of you already know exactly what I\'m talking about.\r\n\r\nIt\'s why you remember that one criticism in a sea of compliments. Why you o=\r\nbsess over the $200 dinner instead of the $20,000 you invested this year.\r\n\r\nYour brain defaults to negative.\r\n\r\nBut you can train it to stop.\r\n\r\n3 steps to overcome your negativity bias\r\n\r\nStep 1: Notice the negative thought\r\n\r\nNext time you react to an idea, like \"I could start a business in 2026,=E2=\r\n=80=9D pause. Notice what thoughts immediately pop up.\r\n\r\n\"I don\'t have time.\" \"What if I fail?\" \"I\'m not ready.\"\r\n\r\nDon\'t judge the thoughts. Just notice them.\r\n\r\nStep 2: Separate the feeling from the thought\r\n\r\nYou feel scared about starting a business. So your brain scrambles to hand =\r\nyou \"logical\" reasons not to do it.\r\n\r\nBut you\'re confusing a feeling (fear of failure) with a thought (reasons yo=\r\nu shouldn\'t start).\r\n\r\nYour brain frantically Googling reasons why you shouldn\'t do the thing.\r\n\r\nThoughts are just ideas.\r\n\r\nOn their own, they=E2=80=99re neutral.\r\n\r\nThey only gain power when you attach them to feelings =E2=80=94 fear, shame=\r\n, urgency, excitement.\r\n\r\nSeparate the two, and you get your leverage back.\r\n\r\nThat leverage is the difference between reacting emotionally and choosing d=\r\neliberately.\r\n\r\nWhen your thought isn=E2=80=99t attached to a feeling, you get to decide wh=\r\nether it deserves action =E2=80=94 or whether it=E2=80=99s just noise.\r\n\r\nStep 3: Decide what to do with the thought\r\n\r\nA therapist once told me: \"You can\'t keep a thought from entering your mind=\r\n, but you don\'t have to sit it down and serve it dinner.\"\r\n\r\nOnce you\'ve noticed the thought and separated the feeling, ask yourself:\r\n\r\n- Is this thought actually valid?\r\n- What if things went the exact opposite way?\r\n- What if this went really, really well?\r\n\r\nLook, our brains are wired for negativity bias. And rewiring these patterns=\r\n takes practice. A lot of it.\r\n\r\nIt=E2=80=99s much easier when you=E2=80=99re not doing it alone.\r\n\r\nWhen you have a community and coaching, you=E2=80=99re surrounded by people=\r\n working on the same things. You can ask questions, get feedback, and have =\r\nsomeone catch you before you spiral or quit.\r\n\r\nThat=E2=80=99s exactly why so many of you keep asking when Earnable Live (h=\r\nttps://d586LZ04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/W5+113/d586LZ04/VWJVH825FTDDN6YlKL=\r\ndJ5Vy1W6mk3Cf5HxRnbN8XrLGM3pyd0W95jsWP6lZ3lwW2G8s2_226SN9W16bK9M5LpNfSW3ZKT=\r\nl47VshMQW2gh